{
  "raw": {
    "https://wnmu.peopleadmin.com/postings/3766": {
      "title": "Nursing - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Western New Mexico University | Nursing - Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Welcome to WNMU Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Nursing - Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Nursing - Assistant Professor Position Classification Faculty Employment Type Full-Time Benefits Full Time Benefitted Department School of Nursing Summary Use appropriate teaching methods to facilitate student learning for Nursing courses. Duties Pre-Licensure BSN Teaching responsibilities are consistent with the New Mexico Nursing Education Consortium ( NMNEC ) guidelines; teaching load may be comprised of face-to-face and/or online course presentation, with clinical, laboratory skills, and simulation lab. Faculty are expected to contribute to instruction within the laboratory and/or simulation setting as necessary while also instructing students within the hospital or other clinical environment. Some work with graduate nursing courses and/or clinicals may be required. Teach courses assigned using standardized nursing curriculum and Canvas Learning Management System ( LMS ). Maintains a safe working environment and complies with all state and federal safety regulations. Participates in departmental meetings and special projects as appropriate. Participates in office hours commensurate with the credit-hour load. Supervises students in class, clinical, and laboratory settings utilizing the policies and procedures in the appropriate student and faculty guidelines for the School of Nursing and the University. Faculty are required to travel to Deming for class, clinical, and simulation at specified times throughout each semester. Works with nursing faculty and the Associate Dean to maintain accreditation standards, documentation, and ongoing quality improvement. Participates in University committees to support the Strategic Plan of the University. Utilizes resources provided to maintain professional development, especially in nursing education. Performs other duties as assigned. Education/Background Master of Science in Nursing ( MSN ) as per accreditation standards. A clinical background in bedside nursing is required. BLS must be current. Active, unencumbered license as a Registered Nurse (RN) with eligibility for RN licensure in the state of New Mexico. Bilingual (Spanish) preferred. Job Knowledge Supervision of nursing students in the clinical setting. Ability to work as a team with other University faculty. Communication skills with critical thinking regarding student supervision. Competence in all nursing skills for the pre-licensure BSN -level student. Must be knowledgeable of university policies and procedures. Must be able to handle multiple deadlines and maintain accuracy. Must be sensitive to cultural differences within the University and community. Fluent in Microsoft Office Applications. Working Conditions/ Physical Demands (With or Without Accommodations) Normal office, may travel some within the community when needed. May be required to transport normal office equipment and materials. Ability to comprehend and work with a variety of information from various sources. Able to clearly communicate with a diverse population of individuals. Ability to compose correspondence and reports and remain in a sedentary position for prolonged periods of time. May be required to work additional hours or days depending on circumstances. Other Requirements a. Valid New Mexico driver’s license. b. Must pass a Defensive Driving Course within 2 months of hire date. c. BLS must be active upon start date. Apply By Location Silver City-On Campus & Deming-On Campus Salary Range $77,773-$84,360 Length of Contract 10 months Advertising Summary Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * Do you have a current BLS? Yes No * Do you have an active unencumbered license as a Registered Nurse (RN) with eligibility for an RN license in the state of New Mexico? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Licensures Optional Documents Western New Mexico University P.O. Box 680 Silver City, NM 88062 Phone 1-800-872-9668 wnmu.edu © 2022 -- Regents of Western New Mexico University • Accessibility • Consumer Information • Mission/Vision • HED Dashboard • Non Discriminatory Notice • Accreditation • Public Record Request • Departmental Peer Review • Title IX – Sexual Misconduct • Contact Us • Admin Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://wnmu.peopleadmin.com/postings/3972": {
      "title": "Bilingual-Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Western New Mexico University | Bilingual-Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Welcome to WNMU Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Bilingual-Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Bilingual-Assistant Professor Position Classification Faculty Employment Type Full-Time Benefits Full Time Benefitted Department College of Education Summary Use appropriate teaching methods to support and magnify student learning for courses in Bilingual Spanish and English Education. Duties Teaches and supervises a 12-credit course load (undergraduate and graduate level) in bilingual education theory and practice, supporting active engagement and learning in online, video-conference, face to face, and hybrid formats. Supervises clinical experiences, face-to-face and/or virtually as needed. Develops syllabi, maintain materials, and supplies for the classes assigned. Collaborates with colleagues in Bilingual/Bicultural curriculum development. Collaborates with area schools and districts, providing professional development and supporting district Bilingual education initiatives. Assists with CAEP and ILC accreditation. Conducts research program or other scholarship activities suitable to a small, teaching university that accommodates the inclusion of undergraduate and graduate students. Provides professional contributions within areas of expertise as appropriate. Participates in departmental and University committees and special projects. Provides a broad range of administrative and supervisory functions. Supervises assigned staff in accordance with WNMU personnel practices including recruitment, training, performance evaluation, guidance, etc. Participates in the process of ongoing personal and professional development. Maintains comprehensive communication among all contacts (internal and external). Models professional standards and ethics in accordance with WNMU philosophy. Performs other duties as assigned. Education/Background Required An earned doctorate in Bilingual Education or related fields ( TESOL , Curriculum and Instruction, Education) or ABD (with graduation date) Demonstrated proficiency as a speaker of Spanish Language Evidence of educational (research or teaching) work and experience in Bilingual Settings. Experience in the Pre-K-12 classroom. Job Knowledge Demonstrated commitment to cultivate an understanding of the rich and varied cultures of New Mexico and to the success of the university’s mission to serve local and global communities. Robust and current formal academic preparation/advanced study in Biliteracy, Bilingualism, Language Education, Language Teacher Preparation preferably linked to New Mexico contexts. Interest in, commitment to, and/or evidence of strong work in community-engaged approaches through outreach, advocacy, and collaboration with rural, frontier and urban communities in New Mexico. Excellent bilingual communication and interpersonal skills Knowledge of and experience with multicultural populations. Knowledge and experience specific to the complexities of teaching in rural and high-poverty schools including students with high-incidence disabilities, and from culturally and linguistically diverse backgrounds. Knowledgeable about research-based practices for preparing quality professionals who can deliver differentiated core standards-based curriculum to students with varied learning and behavior needs. Experience working in diverse ethno-linguistic environments to promote education change and social justice for the success and empowerment of all learners. Experience in teaching online, web-based, and video-conference/zoom environment. Demonstrated potential for contributions to the advancement of equitable education through research, innovative instruction, program development, and service to the community. Must be able to adapt to instructional needs of the department depending on circumstances. Must be knowledgeable of university policies and procedures. Must be able to handle multiple deadlines and maintain accuracy. Must be sensitive to cultural differences within the University and community. Fluent in Microsoft Office Applications. Working Conditions/ Physical Demands (With or Without Accommodations) Normal office environment, may travel some within the community when needed. May be required to transport normal office equipment and materials. Ability to comprehend and work with a variety of information from various sources. Able to clearly communicate with a diverse population of individuals. Ability to compose correspondence and reports and remain in a sedentary position for prolonged periods of time. May be required to work additional hours or days depending on circumstances Other Requirements a. Requires a valid driver’s license. b. Required to complete Defensive Driving Course within 6 months. (If applicable to the role) Apply By Location Silver City-On Campus Salary Range $65,306 w/o terminal degree to $70,837 w terminal degree Length of Contract 9 Months Advertising Summary EEO Statement Western New Mexico University ( WNMU ) provides equal opportunity for employment for all qualified applicants. WNMU prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, spousal affiliation, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal and state law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * What is the highest level of education attained? GED High School Diploma Associates Degree Bachelors Degree Masters Degree PHD * Do you have demonstrated proficiency as a speaker, of Spanish Language? Yes No * Do you have a background in educational work (research or teaching), experience in Pre-K–12 classrooms, and bilingual settings? Note: If you answer \"Yes,\" this experience must be explicitly detailed in both your resume and your application. Yes No * Do you hold an earned doctorate in Bilingual Education or related fields? Yes No * If you are ABD (All But Dissertation), please list your degree and your expected graduation date. Otherwise, please enter \"N/A\": (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Writing Sample Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Teaching Sample Video Optional Documents Western New Mexico University P.O. Box 680 Silver City, NM 88062 Phone 1-800-872-9668 wnmu.edu © 2022 -- Regents of Western New Mexico University • Accessibility • Consumer Information • Mission/Vision • HED Dashboard • Non Discriminatory Notice • Accreditation • Public Record Request • Departmental Peer Review • Title IX – Sexual Misconduct • Contact Us • Admin Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://wnmu.peopleadmin.com/postings/3971": {
      "title": "Photography-Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Western New Mexico University | Photography-Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Welcome to WNMU Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Photography-Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Photography-Assistant Professor Position Classification Faculty Employment Type Full-Time Benefits Full Time Benefitted Department Expressive Arts Summary Use appropriate teaching methods to facilitate student learning in photography and related courses. Lead the photography studio and laboratory, maintaining photography as the primary discipline while supporting potential curriculum development in contemporary lens-based, time-based, and interdisciplinary media. Strengthen the established art program and build connections with Graphic Design, Sculpture, Ceramics, and Painting/Drawing. Duties Teach a 12-credit-hour course load per semester through lectures, studio presentations, demonstrations, and related instruction. Studio courses are 4 credit hours. Conduct meaningful one-on-one and group critiques of student work; mentor students in developing their artistic vision, studio habits, and personal work. Develop and update syllabi, grading rubrics, and studio projects; adapt instruction to departmental needs and contribute to photography and expanded media curriculum development. Advise students pursuing art majors and minors and mentor them in professional photographic practices, careers in art, portfolio development, and exhibitions. Operate and maintain the photography laboratory, equipment, and supplies; maintain a safe studio that complies with applicable state and federal safety regulations. Collaborate with faculty across studio areas to support interdisciplinary projects and student learning. Lead educational art trips to galleries and museums; contribute to summer workshops and Expressive Arts web content as appropriate. Participate in program and studio assessment and use findings to improve instruction and curriculum. Maintain an active creative photography practice and exhibition record; pursue scholarship and professional activities appropriate to a small teaching university, with opportunities for undergraduate participation. Participate in departmental and university committees, special projects, and professional contributions within areas of expertise. Perform assigned administrative and supervisory functions, including supervision of assigned staff under WNMU personnel practices; maintain effective communication, professional development, and professional standards and ethics. Performs other duties as assigned. Education/Background Required Qualifications MFA with an emphasis in Photography, with demonstrated expertise in photography. College teaching experience and a strong, active creative photography practice and exhibition record are required. Applicants must submit a portfolio and examples of student work with their online application. Bilingual proficiency in Spanish is preferred. Preferred Qualifications Experience in: • Analog and darkroom photography • Experimental or alternative photographic processes • Expanded media practices, including time-based media and related approaches • Installation and projection • Mixed-media approaches • Hybrid analog/digital processes • Interdisciplinary approaches to studio practice Bilingual proficiency in Spanish is preferred. Job Knowledge Expert hands-on knowledge of the technical and aesthetic aspects of photography and design, with a broad knowledge of art history and contemporary art. Ability to critique artwork thoughtfully, engage a diverse student population at an open-enrollment university, and collaborate with students, faculty, and campus administration. Positive, supportive interpersonal and communication skills; ability to teach effective studio habits and adapt to departmental instructional needs. Knowledge of university policies and procedures, ability to manage multiple deadlines accurately, and sensitivity to cultural differences within the university and community. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications is required; hands-on Canvas experience and knowledge of current teaching research and pedagogy are desirable.Existing resources include a shared Photography/Graphic Design computer lab, a traditional darkroom, photographic lighting and equipment, institutional software and computer resources, and Webb Theater for projection, installation, critique, and interdisciplinary work. Working Conditions/ Physical Demands (With or Without Accommodations) Normal classroom, office, and photography studio and laboratory environments. May be required to lift and transport photographic equipment and materials. Work includes reading screens and printed materials, communicating with students and colleagues, operating photographic and computer equipment, and identifying equipment or studio conditions requiring attention. Activities may involve typing, writing, standing, reaching, bending, crouching, walking, kneeling, and prolonged sitting. May be required to work additional hours or days depending on circumstances. Other Requirements Apply By Location Silver City-On Campus Salary Range $61,514 w/o terminal degree to $66,724 w terminal degree Length of Contract 9 Months Advertising Summary EEO Statement Western New Mexico University ( WNMU ) provides equal opportunity for employment for all qualified applicants. WNMU prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, spousal affiliation, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal and state law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires both college-level teaching experience and an active, exhibited photography practice. Do you meet both of these requirements? Yes No * Please list which of these you have experience in: • Analog and darkroom photography • Experimental or alternative photographic processes • Expanded media practices, including time-based media and related approaches • Installation and projection • Mixed-media approaches • Hybrid analog/digital processes • Interdisciplinary approaches to studio practice (Open Ended Question) * Do you possess advanced proficiency across all of the following studio practices and techniques? • Photography • Digital editing and photographic workflow • Printing and photographic output • Studio lighting • Photography lab operation and maintenance • Professional photographic practices Yes No * Do you have a MFA with an emphasis in Photography, with demonstrated expertise in photography? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Portfolio Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Optional Documents Western New Mexico University P.O. Box 680 Silver City, NM 88062 Phone 1-800-872-9668 wnmu.edu © 2022 -- Regents of Western New Mexico University • Accessibility • Consumer Information • Mission/Vision • HED Dashboard • Non Discriminatory Notice • Accreditation • Public Record Request • Departmental Peer Review • Title IX – Sexual Misconduct • Contact Us • Admin Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
