licies and procedures, ability to manage multiple deadlines accurately, and sensitivity to cultural differences within the university and community. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications is required; hands-on Canvas experience and knowledge of current teaching research and pedagogy are desirable.Existing resources include a shared Photography/Graphic Design computer lab, a traditional darkroom, photographic lighting and equipment, institutional software and computer resources, and Webb Theater for projection, installation, critique, and interdisciplinary work. Working Conditions/ Physical Demands (With or Without Accommodations) Normal classroom, office, and photography studio and laboratory environments. May be required to lift and transport photographic equipment and materials. Work includes reading screens and printed materials, communicating with students and colleagues, operating photographic and computer equipment, and identifying equipment or studio conditions requiring attention. Activities may involve typing, writing, standing, reaching, bending, crouching, walking, kneeling, and prolonged sitting. May be required to work additional hours or days depending on circumstances. Other Requirements Apply By 01/08/2027 Location Silver City-On Campus Salary Range $61,514 w/o terminal degree to $66,724 w terminal degree Length of Contract 9 Months Advertising Summary EEO Statement Western New Mexico University ( WNMU ) provides equal opportunity for employment for all qualified applicants. WNMU prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, spousal affiliation, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal and state law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * This position requires both college-level teaching experience and an active, exhibited photography practice. Do you meet both of these requirements? Yes No * Please list which of these you have experience in: • Analog and darkroom photography • Experimental or alternative photographic processes • Expanded media practices, including time-based media and related approaches • Installation and projection • Mixed-media approaches • Hybrid analog/digital processes • Interdisciplinary approaches to studio practice (Open Ended Question) * Do you possess advanced proficiency across all of the following studio practices and techniques? • Photography • Digital editing and photographic workflow • Printing and photographic output • Studio lighting • Photography lab operation and maintenance • Professional photographic practices Yes No * Do you have a MFA with an emphasis in Photography, with demonstrated expertise in photography? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Portfolio Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Optional Documents Western New Mexico University P.O. Box 680 Silver City, NM 88062 Phone 1-800-872-9668 wnmu.edu © 2022 -- Regents of Western New Mexico University • Accessibility • Consumer Information • Mission/Vision • HED Dashboard • Non Discriminatory Notice • Accreditation • Public Record Request • Departmental Peer Review • Title IX – Sexual Misconduct • Contact Us • Admin Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
