    "https://wnmu.peopleadmin.com/postings/3996": {
      "title": "Marketing - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Western New Mexico University | Marketing - Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Welcome to WNMU Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Marketing - Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Marketing - Assistant Professor Position Classification Faculty Employment Type Full-Time Benefits Full Time Benefitted Department School of Business Summary The Assistant Professor of Marketing is a full-time, campus-based faculty member who teaches undergraduate and graduate marketing courses and contributes to instruction in related business disciplines according to documented qualifications and School needs. The position advances student success through effective teaching, experiential learning, scholarship, and service. The faculty member strengthens career-focused marketing education, integrates responsible use of business technology, and collaborates on the evaluation and development of potential offerings in applied AI, Management Information Systems ( MIS ), Economics and related business fields. The position supports the School of Business priorities for enrollment and retention, curriculum modernization, employer engagement, assessment, and sustainable program growth. The position supports the strategic direction of the School of Business with his/her expertise in marketing and information analytics. Duties 1. Teach undergraduate and graduate marketing courses, including principles of marketing, consumer behavior, market research, digital and social media marketing, integrated marketing communications, and marketing strategy. Teach other marketing courses as assigned. Carry the assigned teaching load, normally 12 credit hours per semester, subject to WNMU workload policies and approved adjustments. 2. Be willing to teach courses in at least one additional business area for which documented academic or professional preparation supports assignment. Priority areas include business applications of AI, MIS , marketing or business analytics, and digital business; other areas may include introduction to business, business communications, entrepreneurship, economics, or management. 3. Develop and maintain rigorous, accessible courses, syllabi, learning materials, and assessments for face-to-face, online, and hybrid instruction. Maintain an active instructional presence, provide timely feedback and communication, hold office hours, and submit grades and required records on schedule. 4. Integrate current marketing practices, data analysis, business information systems, and responsible AI applications into appropriate courses. Teach students to evaluate technology outputs and make sound decisions while addressing accuracy, privacy, bias, intellectual property, and academic integrity. 5. Collaborate with faculty and School leadership for the ongoing review of the marketing curriculum and evaluate potential degrees, concentrations, certificates, or courses. Especially those that integrate technology through applied AI, MIS , and related fields. Contribute disciplinary expertise, employer input, learning outcomes, course proposals, and resource assessments through established approval processes. 6. Design and supervise experiential learning through employer projects, marketing campaigns, simulations, case analysis, applied research, internships, or competitions. Connect coursework to professional skills, career opportunities, and regional business needs. 7. When appropriate, support student organizations and activities and coordinate with advising and other student support personnel to improve retention and completion. 8. When appropriate, participate in recruitment and outreach activities, including engagement with prospective students, high schools, community colleges, transfer students, and working adults. Collaborate with School personnel to communicate program opportunities and student achievements. 9. Assess course and program learning outcomes, maintain assessment documentation, and use findings to improve instruction and curricula. Contribute to ACBSP accreditation activities, program review, strategic planning, and evidence of continuous improvement. 10. Maintain a program of scholarship appropriate to a teaching-focused university through research, publications, presentations, applied projects, or the scholarship of teaching and learning. Maintain disciplinary currency through professional development and involve students in scholarly work when appropriate. 11. Serve on School and University committees and engage with the university community. WNMU is a central pillar of our local community and faculty regularly engage with employers, alumni, and community partners on educational and professional initiatives. Demonstrate collegiality, ethical conduct, and consistent communication, and complete required administrative responsibilities and training. 12. Performs other duties as assigned. Education/Background Minimum Required Qualifications Earned terminal degree in Marketing, or a closely related field by the appointment start date. Documented preparation to teach in at least one additional business area through relevant graduate coursework, teaching, research, professional practice, or a combination of these. Teaching assignments must satisfy applicable WNMU faculty qualification requirements. Evidence of effective teaching or potential for effective teaching at the university level, including the ability to teach online and engage students from varied backgrounds and levels of preparation. Evidence of scholarship or a viable scholarly agenda, effective written and oral communication, collaborative work, professional experience, and commitment to student mentoring and career preparation. Preferred Qualifications PhD in Marketing or Business Administration with a concentration in Marketing. Demonstrated ability to teach or develop coursework in business applications of AI, MIS , marketing analytics, business analytics, or digital business. Stronger preparation across these priority areas will receive particular consideration. Experience with tools used in marketing and business decision-making, such as customer relationship management systems, digital campaign analytics, spreadsheets, data visualization, or AI-enabled business workflows. Successful undergraduate and graduate teaching; effective online course design and delivery using Canvas or a comparable learning management system. Relevant marketing or business industry experience; employer partnerships, internships, or community projects; and experience with curriculum development, learning assessment, or accreditation. Experience supporting first-generation, rural, Hispanic, transfer, or adult learners. Spanish language proficiency is preferred. Job Knowledge Strong knowledge of marketing theory and practice, including consumer behavior, marketing research, digital marketing, and strategy; ability to apply quantitative and qualitative evidence to business decisions. Working knowledge of responsible AI use and business technology, with the ability to integrate appropriate applications into marketing instruction and develop expertise in related teaching areas. Knowledge of effective university teaching, online learning, accessible course design, assessment, and academic integrity. Ability to support WNMU’s mission and values, learn and follow University policies and procedures, manage competing responsibilities, and work effectively with students, colleagues, employers, and community partners. Working Conditions/ Physical Demands (With or Without Accommodations) Normal office environment, may travel some within the community when needed. May be required to transport normal office equipment and materials. Ability to comprehend and work with a variety of information from various sources. Able to clearly communicate with a diverse population of individuals. Ability to compose correspondence and reports and remain in a sedentary position for prolonged periods of time. May be required to work additional hours or days depending on circumstances. Campus-based responsibilities include classroom instruction, student meetings, and School and University activities in Silver City, New Mexico. Online teaching may be included in the assignment. Must be willing and able to develop and implement a marketing plan for the School of Business, supporting the goals from the strategic plan. Other Requirements Requires a valid driver’s license. Required to complete Defensive Driving Course within 6 months if assigned duties include University-related driving. Apply By Location Silver City-On Campus Salary Range $118,397 Length of Contract 9 Months Advertising Summary EEO Statement Western New Mexico University ( WNMU ) provides equal opportunity for employment for all qualified applicants. WNMU prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, spousal affiliation, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal and state law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you currently hold, or will you complete, a terminal degree in Marketing (or a closely related field) before the start date (Fall 2027)? Yes No * Do you have documented preparation to teach in at least one additional business area, through coursework, research, or experience, that is clearly reflected on both your application and your resume? Yes No * Do you understand that this is a traditional, on-campus faculty position requiring physical, in-person presence for teaching, service, and campus activities, and is not a remote job? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Teaching Sample Video Optional Documents Western New Mexico University P.O. Box 680 Silver City, NM 88062 Phone 1-800-872-9668 wnmu.edu © 2022 -- Regents of Western New Mexico University • Accessibility • Consumer Information • Mission/Vision • HED Dashboard • Non Discriminatory Notice • Accreditation • Public Record Request • Departmental Peer Review • Title IX – Sexual Misconduct • Contact Us • Admin Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://wnmu.peopleadmin.com/postings/3997": {
      "title": "Social Work - Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Western New Mexico University | Social Work - Assistant Professor Skip to Main Content Welcome to WNMU Careers Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Social Work - Assistant Professor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Details Position Information Position Title Social Work - Assistant Professor Position Classification Faculty Employment Type Full-Time Benefits Full Time Benefitted Department School of Social Work Summary Use appropriate teaching methods to facilitate student learning for Social Work courses. THIS POSITION IS ON CAMPUS ONLY . REMOTE IS NOT AN OPTION . Duties Teaching responsibilities consist of 12 credit hours per semester in the BSW and/or MSW core curriculum, electives, and social work field practicum courses using synchronous and asynchronous educational technologies. Serves as Lead Instructor for select social work core and elective courses in areas of expertise, including the development of course syllabi and online course design using department approved course template(s), including mentoring and management of adjunct faculty teaching courses for which the individual serves as Lead Instructor. Advises students for BSW and MSW Social Work degree plans, including professional and career advising in the field of Social Work. Supervises students participating in student-directed research. Attends monthly department meetings and program meetings working in close collaboration with School of Social Work full and part time faculty and staff. Participates in School of Social Work admission process including collaborating with team members to review applications for admission to the program utilizing established admission standards. Models professional standards and ethics in accordance with WNMU philosophy, CSWE standards, and the NASW Code of Ethics. Participates in assessment and reporting in accordance with CSWE , department, and university policies/practices. Participates in timely and professional communication. Conducts research program or other scholarship activities suitable to a small, teaching university that accommodates the inclusion of undergraduate students. Provides professional contributions within areas of expertise as appropriate. Participates in departmental and University committees and special projects. Provides a broad range of administrative and supervisory functions. Supervises assigned staff in accordance with WNMU personnel practices including recruitment, training, performance evaluation, guidance, etc. Participates in the process of ongoing personal and professional development. Maintains comprehensive communication among all contacts (internal and external). Models professional standards and ethics in accordance with WNMU philosophy. Performs other duties as assigned. Education/Background REQUIRED MSW from a CSWE – accredited institution plus a minimum of two years of post – MSW practice experience. Proficiency in the use of online synchronous and asynchronous educational technology is required. Candidates must be eligible for a Social Work licensure in New Mexico. PREFERRED Ph.D. or ABD in Social Work with at least five years of post – MSW practice preferred. Bilingual (Spanish) and experience working with diverse populations preferred. Job Knowledge Must be able to adapt to instructional needs of the department depending on circumstances. Must be knowledgeable of University policies and procedures. Must be able to handle multiple deadlines and maintain accuracy. Must be able to demonstrate cultural competence and humility in accordance with NASW , CSWE , and University standards. Fluent in Microsoft Office Applications and technology typically used in online teaching and learning environments. Working Conditions/ Physical Demands (With or Without Accommodations) Normal office, may travel some within the community when needed. May be required to transport normal office equipment and materials. Ability to comprehend and work with a variety of information from various sources. Able to clearly communicate with a diverse population of individuals. Ability to compose correspondence and reports and remain in a sedentary position for prolonged periods of time. May be required to work additional hours or days depending on circumstances. Other Requirements THIS POSITION IS ON CAMPUS ONLY . REMOTE IS NOT AN OPTION . Apply By Location Silver City-On Campus Salary Range $64,664 w/o terminal degree to $70,141 with terminal degree Length of Contract 9 Months Advertising Summary EEO Statement Western New Mexico University ( WNMU ) provides equal opportunity for employment for all qualified applicants. WNMU prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, pregnancy, national origin, age, ancestry, disability, spousal affiliation, sexual orientation, gender identity, genetic information, veteran status, or any other basis protected by federal and state law. Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have your MSW from a CSWE -accredited institution plus a minimum of two years of post- MSW practice experience? (Please ensure your response accurately mirrors and matches the professional history documented on both your application and resume.) Yes No * How many years of post - MSW practice do you have? (Please ensure your response accurately mirrors and matches the professional history documented on both your application and resume.) (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible for social work licensure in New Mexico? Yes No Documents Needed to Apply Required Documents Resume/CV Cover Letter Unofficial Transcripts Leadership Statement Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Licensures Optional Documents Western New Mexico University P.O. Box 680 Silver City, NM 88062 Phone 1-800-872-9668 wnmu.edu © 2022 -- Regents of Western New Mexico University • Accessibility • Consumer Information • Mission/Vision • HED Dashboard • Non Discriminatory Notice • Accreditation • Public Record Request • Departmental Peer Review • Title IX – Sexual Misconduct • Contact Us • Admin Login To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
